---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { CLI_VERSION, RELEASE_URL, installCommands } from "../content/install";

const description = "Install the free Insidia CLI from GitHub with uv or pipx. Set up a local AI security scan, use the coding agent skill, or run checks in CI. Python 3.12+ required.";
const install = installCommands.uv;
---
<Base title="Install the Insidia CLI & Agent Skill | Insidia Labs" description={description} path="/launch">
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap" style="padding:3rem 0 4rem">
    <h1>Insidia CLI</h1>
    <p class="lede">Insidia scans an AI app and the application around it on your machine and writes one HTML report. The CLI is free. It does not need an account. Insidia Cloud, the hosted attacker, is not open yet.</p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>The current release is <a href={RELEASE_URL}>v{CLI_VERSION}</a>. Python 3.12 or newer. Insidia is not on PyPI.</p>
      <pre class="install-box"><code>{install}</code></pre>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.8rem"><code>pipx install</code> accepts the same URL. <code>insidia --version</code> prints the version and the commit you have.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Upgrade</h2>
      <pre class="install-box"><code>insidia upgrade --check
insidia upgrade</code></pre>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.8rem"><code>--check</code> reports whether a newer release exists. <code>insidia upgrade</code> installs it with uv, pipx, or pip, whichever installed your copy, and keeps your engines. A copy from before 1.0.0 has no <code>upgrade</code> command: rerun the install command with <code>--force</code> once.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Scan</h2>
      <pre class="install-box"><code>insidia init
insidia doctor
insidia scan --policy L1 --yes
insidia report --open</code></pre>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.8rem"><code>insidia init</code> writes a localhost scope. A host other than localhost needs <code>authorized: true</code>, which you set. The scan exits 0 when the policy passes, 1 when a check finds a problem, 2 when the run is incomplete, and 130 when you cancel it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Coding agents</h2>
      <pre class="install-box"><code>npx skills add Rushi-Balapure/Insidia-Labs</code></pre>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.8rem">This needs Node.js 22 or later. Paste: "Test this app with Insidia. Only scan localhost, and open the report when you're done."</p>
      <p>You confirm the hosts. The skill tells the agent not to add a host you did not name and not to paste secrets. <code>insidia mcp</code> is the local MCP server for an agent that speaks MCP. <code>scan</code> does not take a URL.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>CI</h2>
      <p>Install the CLI from a release tag, start your target app, then run <code>insidia scan --policy L1 --json</code>. Preserve <code>.insidia/runs/</code> even when the scan fails. Follow the <a href="/docs/guides/ci/">CI guide</a> for runner setup and artifact steps.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
